       "About the author: Joan Lexau (1929–2023) was a celebrated American children's author; she published over fifty books, including 'Striped Ice Cream' and 'Olaf Reads'.",
       "'Me and the Ecology Bit' is an autobiographical humorous story in which the narrator (Jim) describes his efforts for the environment (ecology).",
       "The central idea: everybody feels the need for ecological balance, but when it comes to doing something, people appear indifferent.",
       "The writer says it is very hard to get people to work for ecology.",
       "His famous statement: \"Nobody is willing to do anything about ecology except me. And again nobody listens to me.\"",
       "The writer goes from house to house, meets people and advises them to work on different problems, but the response is not satisfactory.",
       "For guidance the writer has a plan on which his father worked in his childhood.",
       "The writer uses Sundays for ecology work, because on other days it is hard to find time.",
       "On Sundays the neighbours are found at home because of the weekend holiday.",
       "The writer follows a paper route — he distributes newspapers, which connects him with many houses.",
       "The writer told Mr. Williams not to burn the leaves, as it is bad for the air and ecology.",
