       "'Acceptance Speech' is the Nobel Peace Prize acceptance speech of Aung San Suu Kyi, read at the ceremony by her son Alexander Aris.",
       "Aung San Suu Kyi (born 19 June 1945) is the pro-democracy leader of Burma (Myanmar) and head of the National League for Democracy.",
       "She was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 1991 for her non-violent struggle for democracy and human rights.",
       "She could not attend the ceremony herself because she was under house arrest in Burma at the time.",
       "Her elder son Alexander Aris read the speech at Oslo, Norway, on 10 December 1991 — International Human Rights Day.",
       "Aris described his mother as a 'bright symbol for the plight of all the people of Burma'.",
