       "The famous lines of 'An Essay on Man' are: 'To err is human; to forgive, divine' and 'The proper study of mankind is man'.",
       "He wrote 'Ode on Solitude' at the mere age of 12 (around 1700) — it is the earliest poem preserved in his collected works.",
       "The poem is inspired by a poem of the Roman poet Horace.",
       "An 'ode' is an emotional lyric poem addressed to a subject.",
       "The central idea of the poem is the praise of a simple, contented and self-sufficient rural life.",
       "First stanza: 'Happy the man, whose wish and care / A few paternal acres bound, / Content to breathe his native air, / In his own ground.' — happy is the man whose wishes and cares are limited to a few paternal acres.",
