       "The poem 'The Sleeping Porter' is written by the great Nepali poet Laxmi Prasad Devkota.",
       "Laxmi Prasad Devkota (12 November 1909 – 14 September 1959) is called the 'Mahakavi' of Nepali literature.",
       "He was born at Dhobidhara in Kathmandu.",
       "He obtained his Bachelor's degree from Patna University.",
       "He served as the Education Minister of Nepal in 1957–58.",
       "His famous works are 'Muna Madan' (1936), 'Shakuntala', 'Sulochana', 'Kunjini' and 'Pagal'.",
       "'Muna Madan' is one of the most popular books in Nepali literature.",
