        "Give a detailed explanation of the nazm \"Bijli ka Khamba\".",
        "In this poem, the poet Nida Fazli has satirised modernity. The scene of the poem is a village where an electricity pole is installed. The villagers look at this strange thing with wonder and fear. For them it is a marvel. Through this scene the poet shows that the symbols of progress have reached the village, but people's thinking is still old. The poem contrasts rural simplicity and urban modernity. The poet's satire is on those who consider only external progress as progress. Real progress is the progress of thought and awareness. The language of the poem is simple and easily understood. Beneath the veil of humour there is a deep social message. This poem forces the reader to think while smiling.",
