       "Irfan Siddiqui (pen-name 'Irfan') is a distinguished poet of modern Urdu ghazal — regarded a master of neo-classical ghazal.",
       "His real name was Irfan Ahmad Siddiqui — born 11 March 1939 in Badaun (Uttar Pradesh), died 15 April 2004 in Lucknow.",
       "He rarely attended mushairas, yet by the 1980s he had become a leading poetic voice of the subcontinent.",
       "The famous critic Shamsur Rahman Faruqi said reading his couplets amazes one that poetry of such high standard was written in this era.",
       "His books: 'Canvas' (1978), 'Shab-e-Darmiyan' (1984), 'Saat Samawat' (1992), 'Ishq Nama' (1997), 'Dariya' (1999), 'Mauj-e-Darya' (2005).",
       "He had a deep love for Sanskrit — he translated Kalidasa's play 'Malvika Agnimitr' into Urdu (1983).",
       "Famous sher: 'raat ko jiit to sakta nahin lekin ye charagh / kam se kam raat ka nuqsan bahut karta hai' — hope and resistance.",
       "Famous sher: 'hoshiyari dil-e-nadan bahut karta hai / ranj kam sahta hai elaan bahut karta hai' — satire on the naive heart.",
       "Famous sher: 'uTho ye manzar-e-shab-taab dekhne ke liye / ki nind shart nahin KHwab dekhne ke liye' — an invitation to dream.",
       "Famous sher: 'tum parindon se ziyada to nahin ho aazad / sham hone ko hai ab ghar ki taraf lauT chalo' — the limits of freedom.",
       "Opening of a famous ghazal: 'sukhan mein rang tumhaare khayaal hi ke to hain / ye sab karishme hawa-e-visaal hi ke to hain'.",
       "His ghazal blends classical metres, new metaphors and deep thought.",
       "Metaphors like charagh (lamp), raat (night), hawa (breeze) and KHwab (dream) recur in his couplets.",
       "He was very popular in Pakistan too — his book 'Dariya' was published from there.",
       "His poetry shows, along with love, a glimpse of life's philosophy.",
       "Reading Irfan Siddiqui's ghazal gives a sense of linguistic refinement and lofty thought.",
       "He harmonised the ghazal with the demands of the new age — that is his neo-classical trait.",
       "In exams, his introduction, book names and explanations of famous couplets are always asked.",
       "While explaining his couplets, clarifying the metaphors (charagh, raat) is essential.",
       "Irfan Siddiqui's ghazal carries a message of hope, courage and love of life.",
       "His poetry is an important link carrying forward the tradition of Urdu ghazal.",
       "For students, his ghazal is an excellent example of language and expression.",
       "Word meanings: 'نو کلاسیکی' = नव-शास्त्रीय; 'چراغ' = दीपक; 'نقصان' = हानि; 'مزاحمت' = प्रतिरोध; 'نادانی' = नादानी/मूर्खता; 'منظرِ شب تاب' = रात को जगमगाता दृश्य; 'وصال' = मिलन; 'کرشمے' = चमत्कार; 'تہذیب' = सभ्यता; 'فکر' = चिंतन; 'حوصلہ' = साहस; 'روایت' = परंपरा।"
